\description{
Adds the Projection Extension to a STAC Item, recording the coordinate
reference system and grid geometry of the source data.

STAC requires an Item's \code{geometry} and \code{bbox} to be WGS84 longitude/latitude,
whatever projection the data is actually stored in. The Projection Extension
carries the native CRS alongside it, so a client can locate a pixel or read a
window without opening the file:
\itemize{
\item \strong{\code{proj:code}}: The CRS as an \code{AUTHORITY:CODE} string, e.g. \code{"EPSG:32612"}.
\item \strong{\code{proj:wkt2}}: The CRS as a WKT2 string, for CRSs with no authority code.
\item \strong{\code{proj:projjson}}: The CRS as a PROJJSON object.
\item \strong{\code{proj:geometry}} / \strong{\code{proj:bbox}}: Footprint in the native CRS.
\item \strong{\code{proj:shape}}: Raster dimensions as \code{c(rows, columns)}.
\item \strong{\code{proj:transform}}: The affine transform from pixel to CRS coordinates.
\item \strong{\code{proj:centroid}}: Centroid as WGS84 latitude and longitude.
}

